    <bpmn:process id="W_W1455" name="W1455. Import Letter of Credit (LC) Opening, Amendment &amp; Bank Fee Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Import purchase order confirmed with USD-denominated vendor per W2B; vendor requires LC as payment term; or LC amendment requested by vendor/buyer
Frequency: ~30–50 LC openings/month aligned with import PO schedule; ~5–10 LC amendments/month
Volume: ~400–600 TEUs/month of import goods; each LC typically covers PHP 2.5M–15M (USD 45K–270K) in merchandise; LC bank fees of 0.125–0.25% of LC amount per quarter
Owner: Treasury Analyst
Participants: Treasury Analyst, Import Coordinator, Buyer, CFO (LC approval authority), Issuing Bank, Advising/Confirming Bank
Source: workflow W1455 — Import Letter of Credit (LC) Opening, Amendment &amp; Bank Fee Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1455_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1455_Lane1" name="Import Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1455_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1455_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1455_Lane2" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1455_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1455_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1455_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1455_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1455_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1455_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1455_Start4" name="Import purchase order confirmed with USD-denominated vendor per W2B; vendor requires LC…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1455_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1455_Task5" name="LC opening request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: LC opening request: Import Coordinator submits LC opening request to Treasury after PO confirmation per W2B: (a) LC application form with vendor details, shipment details, commodity description, LC amount (USD), latest shipment date, document requirements (commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificate of origin, insurance certificate); (b) attach approved import PO and proforma invoice; (c) specify LC type (irrevocable, confirmed or unconfirmed, at sight or deferred payment); (d) Treasury verifies import PO approval status, vendor credit terms, and budget allocation
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1455_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1455_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1455_Task6" name="LC approval &amp; issuance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: LC approval &amp; issuance: (a) Treasury Analyst reviews LC request: verifies LC amount against approved PO, confirms availability under BuildRight&#x27;s bank credit line, checks FX rate exposure; (b) LC amount &gt; USD 100K (PHP ~5.6M): CFO approval required; (c) LC amount &gt; USD 500K (PHP ~28M): CEO/Board approval required; (d) Treasury submits LC application to issuing bank via online banking portal; (e) bank reviews BuildRight&#x27;s collateral position and credit line utilization; (f) bank issues LC and transmits SWIFT MT700 to vendor&#x27;s advising bank; (g) Treasury records LC in ERP as contingent liability with bank fees, LC number, and expiry date
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): CFO (if &gt; USD 100K)
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1455_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1455_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1455_Task7" name="LC amendment processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: LC amendment processing: If LC terms require amendment (e.g., shipment date extension, quantity adjustment, price change per vendor negotiation): (a) Buyer or Import Coordinator requests amendment with justification; (b) Treasury submits LC amendment to issuing bank; (c) bank transmits SWIFT MT707 to advising bank; (d) amendment fee (typically USD 50–100) charged by bank; (e) Treasury updates LC record in ERP with amended terms and fee
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1455_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1455_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1455_Task8" name="Document presentation &amp; review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Document presentation &amp; review: Upon shipment, vendor&#x27;s bank presents shipping documents to BuildRight&#x27;s issuing bank: (a) issuing bank sends document copies to Treasury and Import Coordinator for review; (b) verify documents match LC terms: (i) correct quantities and descriptions match PO, (ii) shipment within LC latest shipment date, (iii) documents comply with LC requirements; (c) if discrepancies found: (i) notify vendor&#x27;s bank of discrepancies, (ii) negotiate acceptance or rejection with Buyer, (iii) if acceptable discrepancy: issue discrepancy acceptance; (iv) discrepancy fee (USD 50–150) charged by bank
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1455_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1455_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1455_Task9" name="LC payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: LC payment: Upon compliant document presentation (or discrepancy acceptance): (a) issuing bank debits BuildRight&#x27;s USD account for LC amount; (b) Treasury confirms payment in ERP; (c) system updates import PO payment status per W7; (d) actual FX rate recorded for cost accounting (may differ from hedged rate per W80)
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1455_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1455_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1455_Task10" name="LC fee tracking &amp; cost allocation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: LC fee tracking &amp; cost allocation: Treasury tracks all LC-related fees: (a) opening commission (0.125–0.25% per quarter of LC amount); (b) amendment fee (USD 50–100 per amendment); (c) discrepancy fee (USD 50–150); (d) advising/confirming bank fee; (e) courier fee for physical documents; (f) total LC fees allocated to import PO cost for accurate landed cost per W2B; (g) monthly LC fee report provided to Finance Controller for import cost analysis
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1455_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1455_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1455_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1455_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-295 (ensure controlled execution — FX &amp; Investments (PA-18.3).) | - operational: Treasury Analyst review and approval gate
Owner: Treasury Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1455_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1455_Annotation12" targetRef="W1455_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1455_Flow14" sourceRef="W1455_Start4" targetRef="W1455_Task5" />
