    <bpmn:process id="W_W1473" name="W1473. FX Hedge Effectiveness Testing, Mark-to-Market Valuation &amp; Accounting Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Month-end accounting close; or significant FX rate movement (&gt; 2% in a week); or quarterly hedge effectiveness assessment
Frequency: Monthly mark-to-market; quarterly hedge effectiveness testing; ad-hoc for significant FX movements
Volume: ~10–15 active FX forward contracts at any time; ~PHP 1.4B/month in import-related FX exposure
Owner: Treasury Manager
Participants: Treasury Analyst, Controller, External Auditor, CFO
Source: workflow W1473 — FX Hedge Effectiveness Testing, Mark-to-Market Valuation &amp; Accounting Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1473_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1473_Lane1" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1473_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1473_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1473_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1473_Lane2" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1473_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1473_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1473_Lane3" name="Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1473_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1473_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1473_Start5" name="Month-end accounting close; or significant FX rate movement (&gt; 2% in a week); or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1473_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1473_Task6" name="Monthly mark-to-market valuation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly mark-to-market valuation (during month-end close per W86): (a) Treasury Analyst retrieves current FX forward rates from bank counterparties for all open contracts: remaining tenor, contracted rate vs. current market rate, notional amount; (b) calculates unrealized gain/loss per contract: (contracted rate − current forward rate) × notional amount; (c) aggregates total mark-to-market position across all open contracts; (d) records MTM adjustment in GL: Dr./Cr. Derivative Financial Asset/Liability, Cr./Dr. Other Comprehensive Income (effective hedge) or P&amp;L (ineffective hedge portion)
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1473_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1473_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1473_Task7" name="Settlement of maturing contracts">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Settlement of maturing contracts: (a) when an FX forward contract matures: (i) bank settles the contract — BuildRight buys/sells foreign currency at contracted rate; (ii) Treasury Analyst verifies settlement amount matches contract terms; (iii) realized gain/loss = difference between contracted rate and spot rate at inception; (iv) system records: Dr. Cash (USD), Cr./Dr. Cash (PHP), Cr./Dr. Realized FX Gain/Loss; (b) Treasury Analyst reconciles settled contract with original hedge documentation (hedged item, risk, strategy) per PFRS 9 requirements
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2 hours/settlement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1473_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1473_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1473_Task8" name="Quarterly hedge effectiveness testing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly hedge effectiveness testing: (a) Treasury Manager performs hedge effectiveness assessment using dollar-offset method: (i) cumulative change in fair value of hedging instrument ÷ cumulative change in fair value of hedged item = hedge ratio; (ii) hedge is effective if ratio is between 80% and 125% (PFRS 9 bright-line test); (b) if hedge fails effectiveness test: (i) reclassify deferred OCI amounts to P&amp;L, (ii) assess whether hedging relationship should be discontinued, (iii) document reason for ineffectiveness (e.g., hedged item partially settled, timing mismatch); (c) prospective effectiveness: assess whether hedging strategy remains appropriate for next quarter based on updated import forecasts per W31
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1473_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1473_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1473_Task9" name="PFRS 9 disclosure preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: PFRS 9 disclosure preparation: (a) Controller compiles FX hedge disclosures for quarterly and annual financial statements: (i) hedging instruments: notional amounts, fair values, remaining maturities, (ii) hedge effectiveness results, (iii) amounts reclassified from OCI to P&amp;L, (iv) ineffectiveness gains/losses recognized in P&amp;L; (b) External Auditor reviews hedge documentation and effectiveness testing as part of annual audit per W86
Responsible (R): Controller / External Auditor
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1473_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1473_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1473_Task10" name="FX exposure monitoring &amp; hedge adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: FX exposure monitoring &amp; hedge adjustment: (a) if PHP/USD moves &gt; 2% in a week: Treasury Manager reassesses hedge coverage — is the current hedge ratio adequate for remaining import exposure? (b) if import forecast changes significantly (new large vendor order, cancelled shipment): adjust hedge position — roll forward contract, enter new contract, or allow partial hedge lapse per W80; (c) document hedge adjustments with updated hedge documentation per PFRS 9
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per trigger</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1473_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1473_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1473_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1473_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-295 (ensure controlled execution — FX &amp; Investments (PA-18.3).) | - operational: Treasury Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Treasury Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1473_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1473_Annotation12" targetRef="W1473_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1473_Flow14" sourceRef="W1473_Start5" targetRef="W1473_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1473_Flow15" sourceRef="W1473_Task6" targetRef="W1473_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1473_Flow16" sourceRef="W1473_Task7" targetRef="W1473_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1473_Flow17" sourceRef="W1473_Task8" targetRef="W1473_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1473_Flow18" sourceRef="W1473_Task9" targetRef="W1473_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1473_Flow19" sourceRef="W1473_Task10" targetRef="W1473_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1473_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1473_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1473">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1473_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1473_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1473_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1473_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
