    <bpmn:process id="W_W5541" name="W5541. Bank-Failure &amp; Frozen-Deposit Contingency" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A bank holding BuildRight operating accounts, payroll funding accounts, or W318/W1474 placements is placed under BSP/PMC intervention (receivership, conservatorship), freezes withdrawals, or suffers an outage exceeding 24 hours that blocks collections or disbursements
Frequency: Rare; expected &lt; 1 material event per year chain-wide (mid-size Philippine bank failures have occurred — Export Bank, LBC Bank precedents per W1474&#x27;s counterparty canon)
Volume: 1 bank event × all exposed balances (operating accounts, payroll funding accounts, time placements) × the next-10-business-day disbursement calendar (payroll funding per W10/W5540, AP per W556, LC obligations per W1455)
Owner: Treasury Manager
Participants: CFO, Treasury Analyst, Finance Controller, AP Manager (payment rerouting per W556), Payroll Manager (payroll funding per W5540), Legal (PDIC claims, contract review), Trade Finance (LC lines per W1455), Internal Audit (loss assessment), BCP Manager (W848 linkage if service-wide), relationship banks (alternate-channel activation)
Source: workflow W5541 — Bank-Failure &amp; Frozen-Deposit Contingency</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5541_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5541_Lane1" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5541_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5541_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5541_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5541_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5541_Lane2" name="Treasury">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5541_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5541_Lane3" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5541_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5541_Lane4" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5541_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5541_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5541_Start6" name="A bank holding BuildRight operating accounts, payroll funding accounts, or W318/W1474…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5541_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5541_Task7" name="Exposure census (first 24 h)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Exposure census (first 24 h): enumerate every exposure at the affected bank — operating/collections accounts, payroll funding accounts, W318 time placements, W1474 money-market positions, standby LCs/collaterals posted; classify insured (≤ PHP 500K per depositor per bank per PDIC) vs uninsured; freeze any pending instructions to the affected bank
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 4–8 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5541_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5541_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5541_Task8" name="Cash-flow impact assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cash-flow impact assessment: map the next-10-business-day calendar against stranded funds — payroll funding dates (W10 cycle), AP runs (W556), tax remittances, LC settlements/amortization (W1455/W319); quantify the gap: obligations due vs accessible cash; classify severity (days-of-cover lost)
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5541_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5541_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5541_Task9" name="Rerouting activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Rerouting activation: execute the diversification policy&#x27;s alternate-bank channel — switch collections sweeps and remittance-in instructions to alternate banks; redirect payroll funding accounts (notifying the W5540 chain); re-point AP disbursement files in W556; temporary intra-group funding per the VS-72 shared-services intercompany mechanics if the gap exceeds accessible cash; update bank-file formats/mandates with the alternate banks
Responsible (R): Treasury / AP Manager / Payroll Manager
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 2–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5541_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5541_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5541_Task10" name="PDIC claims &amp; recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: PDIC claims &amp; recovery: Legal + Treasury prepare and file PDIC deposit-insurance claims for covered accounts within the claims window; document the insured/uninsured split; uninsured balances → loss assessment, write-off approval per the W81-class write-off policy with Audit sign-off; pursue set-off/recourse positions per deposit contracts
Responsible (R): Legal / Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–8 weeks elapsed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5541_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5541_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5541_Task11" name="Counterparty &amp; policy review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Counterparty &amp; policy review: recalibrate W1474 counterparty limits and the investment policy&#x27;s per-bank concentration caps (post-event lesson: e.g. per-bank cap ≤ 25% of liquid holdings, placements only at banks above an asset-quality floor); re-paper mandates and signatories at alternate banks; confirm no other bank breaches the recalibrated limits
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager / CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5541_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5541_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5541_Task12" name="Governance, disclosure &amp; board reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Governance, disclosure &amp; board reporting: materiality assessment per the W5017 disclosure-controls canon (a listed-company material event if losses/gaps cross thresholds); Audit Committee report with loss quantification and policy changes; lender notification if covenant-relevant (liquidity representations per W319); post-event review feeding the VS-21.2 risk register and KRI thresholds
Responsible (R): CFO / VP Legal / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Accountable (A): Audit Committee
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5541_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5541_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5541_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5541_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-295 (ensure controlled execution — FX &amp; Investments (PA-18.3).); CTL-60 (ensure investment policy compliance.) | - operational: no standing instruction to an intervention-affected bank executes after the freeze flag; every rerouting step is dual-confirmed (Treasury + Finance Controller) | - operational: uninsured balances are written off only via the W81-class approval path with Audit sign-off
Owner: Treasury Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5541_Assoc15" sourceRef="W5541_Annotation14" targetRef="W5541_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5541_Flow16" sourceRef="W5541_Start6" targetRef="W5541_Task7" />
